		display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;
	}
	
	.custom-btn {
		background: #00599c; color: white !important; border: 2px solid #04386D; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px 20px; text-align: center; text-decoration: none !important; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; font-size: 18px; cursor: pointer; transition: 0.3s ease; width: 100%; min-height: 50px; box-sizing: border-box;
	}
	
	.custom-btn:hover {
		background: #04386D; color: white;
	}

</style><p>The GIS Division provides digital data and mapping products for the City of Midland and the general public. Our goal is to provide data in a usable, coherent format for our citizens, consultants, developers, real estate agents, and engineers.</p><p>Midland&apos;s GeoStation is your portal to Midland&apos;s geospatial data. Explore, visualize, and download location-based data about our city through interactive maps, apps, and more. Discover insights about West Texas&apos;s energy hub and uncover the spatial stories that make Midland unique.</p><div class="btn-container"><div class="btn-item"><a href="https://geostation-comgis.hub.arcgis.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" class="custom-btn">GeoStation Open Data Hub</a>&nbsp;</div></div><p><br></p><p><strong>Our data is available in the following formats:</strong></p><h2 class="subhead1">GIS Data</h2><p><strong>NOTICE: This data is copyrighted by the City of Midland unless otherwise indicated. The City of Midland shall not be responsible for any decisions based upon the use of this data. While this information is made available to the public, it was created for internal use by the City of Midland, and, while we make every attempt to keep it updated, we make no claim as to its accuracy or completeness. This data is not designed to be used as a primary tool in permitting, citing, or in other decisions based solely on this information.</strong></p><p>Data is in ESRI Shapefile format and AutoCAD 2007 DWG formats. The files have been zipped to enable faster download times.</p><ul><li>Use <a href="http://usa.autodesk.com/adsk/servlet/pc/index?siteID=123112&id=6703438">Autodesk DWG TrueView</a> program, which is <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/viewers">available for download</a>.</li><li>Use <a href="https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9PLXRWKXXJ21?hl=en-us&gl=US">ArcGIS Explorer</a> to view Shapefiles, which is <a href="https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9PLXRWKXXJ21?hl=en-us&gl=US">available for download</a>.</li><li>The spatial reference of the data is NAD 1983 State Plane Texas Central FIPS 4203 Feet.</li></ul>
    </div>

